{
    "word": "languor",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                "word": "languor",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2a7e7ecd-c6f0-4784-873c-b3720edf84d8",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "languors"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9004a1aa-0c13-3230-bdc3-73877a7e16aa",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A state of the body or mind caused by exhaustion or disease and characterized by a languid or weary feeling; lassitude; (countable) an instance of this."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b28a2dc9-0695-4ad6-85ee-6a903d4598ff",
                                "sense_id": "9004a1aa-0c13-3230-bdc3-73877a7e16aa",
                                "text": "languor of convalescence"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f55d506-4d28-45c6-a1c0-e2f0fadb2b08",
                                "sense_id": "9004a1aa-0c13-3230-bdc3-73877a7e16aa",
                                "text": "Sometimes my pulse beat so quickly and hardly, that I felt the palpitation of every artery; at others, I nearly sank to the ground through languor and extreme weakness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdb59711-824d-46e7-baf6-5df221d1bd95",
                                "sense_id": "9004a1aa-0c13-3230-bdc3-73877a7e16aa",
                                "text": "As the opinion announcements have stretched past the half-hour mark, some in the public gallery exhibit a bit of languor, but they perk up when [U.S. Supreme Court Justice Elena] Kagan begins discussing western gray squirrels."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39cc57b4-d115-3802-9439-f1b86bc844a8",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Melancholy caused by lovesickness, sadness, etc.; (countable) an instance of this."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d34105f2-92d3-30a5-ae0b-da7362901b95",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dullness, sluggishness; lack of vigour; stagnation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e06abb7-58d5-468d-9e72-cfa132ce7eb5",
                                "sense_id": "d34105f2-92d3-30a5-ae0b-da7362901b95",
                                "text": "I rushed towards her, and embraced her with ardour; but the deathly languor and coldness of the limbs told me, that what I now held in my arms had ceased to be the Elizabeth whom I had loved and cherished."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53a22620-f256-470f-96f0-5140a21595b3",
                                "sense_id": "d34105f2-92d3-30a5-ae0b-da7362901b95",
                                "text": "From languor she passed to the lightest vivacity; her temper became merry and wild in the extreme; she was all at once a tease, a tomboy, and a witch."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b20aa01-8995-3ee8-92a8-a688455c334e",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Listless indolence or inactivity, especially if enjoyable or relaxing; dreaminess; (countable) an instance of this."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cee117d-203c-4266-9794-9aa1201bf481",
                                "sense_id": "8b20aa01-8995-3ee8-92a8-a688455c334e",
                                "text": "It is earth's brief breathing space, after the heat and hurry of her busier time; like that repose known only to the young and happy, when the nerves gradually compose themselves, the thoughts gather into some vague but delicious train, and the eyes are closed by languor before sleep."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81ad8403-8c62-4f49-9e57-b562f282660b",
                                "sense_id": "8b20aa01-8995-3ee8-92a8-a688455c334e",
                                "text": "The languor of Youth—how unique and quintessential it is! How quickly, how irrecoverably lost! The zest, the generous affections, the illusions, the despair, all the traditional attributes of Youth—all save this—come and go with us through life; [...] but languor—the relaxation of yet unwearied sinews, the mind sequestered and self-regarding, the sun standing still in the heavens and the earth throbbing to our own pulse—that belongs to Youth alone and dies with it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65754ccb-6fce-4cf4-897b-5e0dafa7e28d",
                                "sense_id": "8b20aa01-8995-3ee8-92a8-a688455c334e",
                                "text": "Repose! The very word has a nostalgic ring to it, conjuring up a vanished world of pale solitude, gentle distances, summer vistas, languour, and lovely women …"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a24ccf5d-1b35-3fed-aaea-c3f0259b7ca9",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Heavy humidity and stillness of the air."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33200253-02ae-4209-87e1-0202811ff0f6",
                                "sense_id": "a24ccf5d-1b35-3fed-aaea-c3f0259b7ca9",
                                "text": "There is a languor in the air which encourages your own, and the poetry of memory is in every drooping flower and falling leaf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db180e1f-c4a1-4d21-91ee-e65a0c07eeda",
                                "sense_id": "a24ccf5d-1b35-3fed-aaea-c3f0259b7ca9",
                                "text": "[A] certain languor in the air hinted at an early summer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13e340b8-7c21-4e0d-ad73-99e030a5b630",
                                "sense_id": "a24ccf5d-1b35-3fed-aaea-c3f0259b7ca9",
                                "text": "The evening was mild, with a certain languor in the air."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "603f3d16-0e06-34c4-a320-e1f4042d9098",
                        "entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sorrow; suffering; also, enfeebling disease or illness; (countable, obsolete) an instance of this."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4bb704f2-8124-4d9d-99a2-9116407199e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "source_sense_description": "state of the body or mind caused by exhaustion or disease and characterized by a languid feeling; an instance of this — see also lassitude",
                        "target_lang_word": "loomheid",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loomheid",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d8dcc8c-e521-3d85-a976-edb9b6b9fc89",
                                        "entry_id": "b3578f37-04e3-3430-af2a-626fdaac54df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "het vermoeid, lui en loom zijn zowel geestelijk als lichamelijk"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90ec2852-96c0-4f62-9af7-2d5ffb2f89d7",
                                                "sense_id": "7d8dcc8c-e521-3d85-a976-edb9b6b9fc89",
                                                "text": "De zon laat de loomheid indalen in elke vezel en porie; alle stress en spanning glijden uit mijn systeem. Zon, zee, wijn en tapas, meer heeft een mens blijkbaar niet nodig om te ontspannen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b438446-1cb6-41f0-a86e-18f377eec01f",
                                                "sense_id": "7d8dcc8c-e521-3d85-a976-edb9b6b9fc89",
                                                "text": "Zorg dat je mee gaat met het seizoen: kruip uit je winterslaap, schud de loomheid van je af en zorg dat je in de volgende versnelling komt. Hoe eerder je dat doet, hoe meer je al gaat genieten. Zo ben jij straks helemaal klaar voor de zomer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c14bb5bd-6fba-4048-bff7-2b4dedc5d56c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b072a133-6409-3588-8abe-70fcad531b5c",
                        "source_sense_description": "state of the body or mind caused by exhaustion or disease and characterized by a languid feeling; an instance of this — see also lassitude",
                        "target_lang_word": "langueur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "langueur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08dc1675-e37b-3334-af9e-75b83749bfc2",
                                        "entry_id": "b91cefa5-c05c-33c6-b86b-ea7ab0356347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affaiblissement physique et moral qui réduit considérablement les forces et l’activité d'une personne. Action, fait de languir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2a7a781-b8cc-43e4-b49c-ced814f96930",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc1675-e37b-3334-af9e-75b83749bfc2",
                                                "text": "Les Liméniennes ont toutes de belles couleurs, […], des yeux noirs d’une expression indéfinissable d’esprit, de fierté et de langueur ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14629261-5614-4ec6-804e-0f9def19ee54",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc1675-e37b-3334-af9e-75b83749bfc2",
                                                "text": "Les sanglots longs\nDes violons\nDe l’automne\nBlessent mon cœur\nD’une langueur\nMonotone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ead47063-e1e4-4b19-a131-864d08e5d48d",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc1675-e37b-3334-af9e-75b83749bfc2",
                                                "text": "Un long baiser rescella leur pacte. Aïssa, lourde de langueur, avait renversé sa tête sur l’épaule de son amant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ea24fef-6a70-45a2-b4a5-4f280549d422",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc1675-e37b-3334-af9e-75b83749bfc2",
                                                "text": "Marguerite tombait en langueur. Elle travaillait toujours et personne ne pouvait lui faire de gros reproches à ce sujet, mais elle travaillait sans joie, d’une allure lasse, comme à regret."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9276d1ab-b6be-49e6-801f-8a31ab0fb0eb",
                                                "sense_id": "08dc1675-e37b-3334-af9e-75b83749bfc2",
                                                "text": "Atteint d’un mal nommé porphyrie, le pauvre garçon est contraint de s’abreuver de sang humain pour conjurer sa langueur chronique."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                        "entry_id": "b91cefa5-c05c-33c6-b86b-ea7ab0356347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État d’abattement d’une personne faible et malade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e102db57-1e03-466a-a45a-ee5586bc4517",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "Il ne sent point les langueurs de l’âge."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2973320-01d8-4403-87b6-c55def201fbf",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "Maladie de langueur (On l’employait dans ce sens au pluriel)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87508e7e-c050-4d34-9277-ed7d7540ba0f",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "Louis XIII tomba dans un grand fauteuil garni d’oreillers, demanda et but un verre d’élixir préparé pour le fortifier contre les évanouissements fréquents que lui causait sa maladie de langueur, fit un geste pour éloigner tout le monde, et seul avec Richelieu, lui parla d’une voix languissante."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec8969e0-467e-4558-a0d5-ab21fd6fe71c",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "Il y a deux ans, la reine le fit appeler pour soigner le dauphin atteint d’une maladie de langueur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11d44b02-c598-40bf-bb6b-2f7bfcde9302",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "Mais j’appréhende de leur être à charge, de devenir paralytique ou aveugle, ou de tomber dans l’enfance, ou encore de souffrir longtemps de quelque maladie de langueur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e4994a9-8fa0-4182-a03b-14b0bee001da",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "— Tranquillisez-vous, ma petite. C’est un peu de langueur. Dans deux jours vous serez sur pied. Reposez-vous. Vous prendrez votre potion, bien sagement, comme je vous l’ai ordonné… N’est-ce pas ? Vous me le promettez ?…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ecb59ee-3c12-4e3e-8e12-cdb722f4b515",
                                                "sense_id": "7d223167-ad41-37d1-b4f9-e4fe20bf71b7",
                                                "text": "Ce qu’il appelle le «languishing», ou la langueur en français, c’est le sentiment de stagner, une profonde impression de vide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d44e614d-b23f-3c13-8cf9-ecd60f4e0634",
                                        "entry_id": "b91cefa5-c05c-33c6-b86b-ea7ab0356347",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cause d’abattement et de nature physique (maladie ou blessure)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5797a5f-f489-4a6f-9b4f-016035daa930",
                                                "sense_id": "d44e614d-b23f-3c13-8cf9-ecd60f4e0634",
                                                "text": "[…]; encore sa vie fut-elle accidentellement écourtée, puisqu’il périt « de langueur » un an après avoir été éborgné par un corbeau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
